The function does a single pointer check and a store, so it can't account for any meaningful share of the 269.94 ms. The change below only adds a branch-prediction hint on the cold error path. Expect no measurable speedup; the time is spent elsewhere in the decoder.

```cpp
void Decode::IncompleteStream()
{
    // Do not allow changing the settings after Read has started.
#if defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)
    if (__builtin_expect(file != NULL, 0))
#else
    if (file != NULL)
#endif
    {
        throw RuntimeException("Can't set incompleteStream option after Decode started!");
    }
    // Don't raise an error if eof is encountered during decode,
    // caller may try to resume if more bytes arrive.
    streamIsComplete = FIT_FALSE;
}
```